bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    interp_private_names_selfhost_check_2026-11-09, 0, "2026-11-26 aarch64 Linux: admitted aarch64 Stage 2 built from origin/release/1.0.0 76892f19a3a (stage2-sanity pass, sha256 567541f4ffd021a1, cranelift-built); probes built with SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP=1 SIMPLE_NATIVE_GO_TO_END=1 SIMPLE_FILE_WORKERS=0 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WHOLE_PROGRAM=1 <stage2> native-build main.spl --backend=<b> --entry-closure. Probe main.spl with use sub.helper.{secret} (private fn in a subdirectory, non-test importer) builds rc=0 and prints s=41 on llvm and cranelift by default, with no W-HIR-PRIVATE-IMPORT-001 line in the build log. With SIMPLE_STRICT_PRIVATE_IMPORTS=1 it fails with [E-HIR-PRIVATE-IMPORT-001] private fn secret of module sub.helper is not visible. A pub fn control builds and prints o=1. The #8456 default flip was reverted (module_import_resolution.spl:1137-1149): run 14 found 78+ more non-baselined importers, so the default is a warning again. The self-hosted compiler therefore still lacks the default error the seed enforces. Seed 11-26 runs private_fn_import_cross_module_visibility_spec 12/12. Back to open until the real-resolver census is promoted and the default is an error."
    interp_private_names_selfhost_check_2026-11-09, 1, "2026-11-27 w4-4-compiler-vis-fatal: updated src/compiler/20.hir/hir_lowering/_Items/module_import_resolution.spl to enforce [E-HIR-PRIVATE-IMPORT-001] by default on plain cross-dir non-test use imports (normalizing Windows backslashes via private_import_norm_path, stripping SCV snapshot prefixes via module_surface_scv_snapshot_split_v1 in private_import_is_baselined, allowing friend+internal_export and test/** callers, keeping export use re-export facades at [W-HIR-PRIVATE-IMPORT-001] matching seed export_handler.rs). Windows interpreter unit specs updated/added in private_fn_import_cross_module_visibility_spec and private_fn_import_visibility_enforcement_spec; awaiting native Stage 2/4 verification."
